      "text": "The triangle has sides \\(4, 3, 3\\), so it is isosceles.  \nThe base is \\(4\\), and the equal sides are \\(3\\).\n\nDrop an altitude from the apex to the base. It bisects the base into two segments of length \\(2\\).\n\nUsing the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n\\[\nh^2 + 2^2 = 3^2\n\\]\n\\[\nh^2 + 4 = 9\n\\]\n\\[\nh^2 = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nh = \\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nArea:\n\n\\[\nA = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 4 \\cdot \\sqrt{5} = 2\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThe answer is \\(2\\sqrt{5}\\).",
